//
// A WIDENING INTO A NULLABLE TIES A WIDENING INTO A RANGE (`@FR-Disp-Ambiguous`, ranked by
// `@FR-Disp-Specific`'s "a nullability step adds to the base rank"): a `u8` into `u8?` is EXACT
// plus the N-Intro step (WIDENED), a `u8` into `integer` is WIDENED with no step, so the two
// members rank alike and the call is refused naming both.  One refusal per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names both members.
// HOLDS: the tie is the call's, not the set's: a `u8?` argument reaches `an(u8?)` EXACT.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `an(u8)` is ambiguous — it is taken by an(integer) and an(u8?)

fn an(x: integer) -> text { "integer {x}" }
fn an(x: u8?) -> text { "u8? {x}" }

fn main() {
  b: u8 = 7;
  println(an(b));
}
